{"name":"Wine Stain","hex":"#69444f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting grape juice, with an ABV ranging from 5.5–16%.","An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting other substances, producing a similar ABV."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entertain (someone) with wine.","To drink wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine"},{"term":"stain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A discolored spot or area caused by spillage or other contact with certain fluids or substances.","A blemish on one's character or reputation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To discolor, as by spilling or other contact with a fluid or substance.","To taint or tarnish someone's character or reputation"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Port-wine stain","blocks":[{"text":"A port-wine stain is a discoloration of the human skin caused by a vascular anomaly. They are so named for their coloration, which is similar in color to port wine, a fortified red wine from Portugal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/PortWineStainHand.jpg/330px-PortWineStainHand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port-wine_stain","wikidata":"Q1409611"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine","wikidata":"Q282"},{"title":"Stain","blocks":[{"text":"A stain is a discoloration that can be clearly distinguished from the surface, material, or medium it is found upon. They are caused by the chemical or physical interaction of two dissimilar materials. Accidental staining may make materials appear used, degraded or permanently unclean. Intentional staining is used in biochemical research, and for artistic effect, such as in wood staining, rust staining and stained glass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Patternspage.jpg/330px-Patternspage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stain","wikidata":"Q2733470"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red","wikidata":"Q3014419"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/RIAN_archive_359290_Mikhail_Gorbachev.jpg/500px-RIAN_archive_359290_Mikhail_Gorbachev.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/RIAN_archive_359290_Mikhail_Gorbachev.jpg/1280px-RIAN_archive_359290_Mikhail_Gorbachev.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/RIAN_archive_359290_Mikhail_Gorbachev.jpg/500px-RIAN_archive_359290_Mikhail_Gorbachev.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mikhail Gorbachev, last leader of the Soviet Union, with a prominent port-wine stain on his forehead","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARIAN_ar